<p>Pope Leo XIV arrived in Algiers on 13 April for the first papal visit to Algeria, opening an 11-day trip that will also take him to Cameroon, Angola, and Equatorial Guinea. His stop in Algeria includes a Mass at the Basilica of Our Lady of Africa and a visit to Souk Ahras, a place tied to St. Augustine of Hippo and the Augustinian order Leo belongs to. The tour is meant to draw attention to Africa’s growing importance to the Catholic Church, where the faith is expanding faster than in other regions. Throughout the trip, Leo is expected to stress peace while meeting political leaders and small but symbolically important Catholic communities in places such as Algeria.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JehAvHh8uI7VrMLIssedEypxWQ6naHfg-pnZeHJEkLlp9LASjr-rup1VxofHkmtBcgsbMytPsb8Xc5MhW3k_-Idy28kcL6sZzX7tmleDTfoKDwwsC2sFnqnp8ulqOMhri_1o9IUDJWQJHjrYCjZAswHQ_HyIgVPta83PvRGWecuqpec_r6gFhKguNz-7maUqNoaf88M8BQR53Cj9ayU' alt='Pope Leo arriving on Monday for a visit with President Abdelmadjid Tebboune of Algeria at the presidential palace in Algiers.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Rain-soaked Mass: Leo celebrated a historic Mass in rainy conditions at the Basilica of Our Lady of Africa in Algiers on 14 April, the ceremonial centerpiece of the Algeria stop.</li><li>Longest trip: The four-country journey from 13 to 23 April is Leo’s longest foreign trip since his election in May 2025.</li><li>Vulnerability focus: The tour is meant to highlight Leo’s attention to some of the Church’s most vulnerable members on the world’s poorest continent.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Vatican aide: An aide said Leo wants to focus the world’s attention on Africa because the continent is vital to the Church’s future. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg0jyx4qq7o'>BBC</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: The newspaper highlighted the contrast Leo is expected to navigate on the tour, from enthusiastic Catholic crowds to authoritarian leaders. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/13/world/europe/pope-leo-africa-future.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Andrey Maslov: The Russian academic said the Vatican needs an independent policy and a stronger foothold in Africa amid strained relations across the West. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/africa/638352-pope-leo-africa-tour/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Theologians cited by coverage: Some theologians said Leo’s reading of Augustine helps explain how he approaches political questions and public criticism. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/14/world/africa/pope-leo-algeria-africa-visit.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg0jyx4qq7o'>Leo becomes first Pope to visit Algeria at start of major Africa tour</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/04/14/pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-historic-mass-at-rainsoaked-basilica-in-algiers'>Pope Leo XIV celebrates historic Mass at rain‑soaked Basilica in Algiers</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/13/pope-leo-visits-algeria-africa-tour-catholic-church'>Pope Leo visits Algeria in sign of Africa’s growing importance to Catholic church</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/with-algeria-visit-pope-leo-returns-to-his-augustinian-roots'>With Algeria visit, Pope Leo returns to his Augustinian roots</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/africa/638352-pope-leo-africa-tour/'>Why is Pope Leo XIV going to Africa?</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/13/world/europe/pope-leo-africa-future.html'>Pope Leo Heads to Africa to Meet the Future of Catholicism</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://apnews.com/article/africa-pope-leo-algeria-muslim-migration-ccf9458e288db4355f359ddf56668caf'>Pope Leo XIV arrives in Algiers, marking the first papal visit to Algeria. He will visit Souk Ahras, the birthplace and home of St. Augustine of Hippo, namesake of the Au